The old executable put back over a database a newer release migrated.
Release 5 changed nothing: release 4's executable opens it as it is, and
the database stays at release 5. Release 6 added a column: release 4's
executable is refused, rather than drop it.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'soup');
PRAGMA user_version = 5;

== after
-- @release 4
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== after
-- @release 6
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, note TEXT) STRICT;

== after
-- @release 4
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

